1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Four to one. That's one in four, right?

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,000
No. Odds count the ways to lose against the ways to win.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Four ways to lose, one way to win. Five outcomes.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,800
One in five. Twenty percent, not twenty-five.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:21,600
Now read a whole betting board that way.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,200
Fifty, twenty-five, twenty and ten percent.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:32,000
That adds to a hundred and five. Only one of them can win.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,800
Those five extra points are the margin, printed on the board.
